      "extract": "Giraud introduced gerbes in order to achieve a geometrical understanding of \\emph{non-abelian} cohomology \\cite{giraud}. However, already \\emph{abelian} gerbes turned out to be interesting: Brylinski introduced the notion of a \\emph{connection} on an abelian gerbe, and showed that these represent classes in a certain \\emph{differential} cohomology theory, namely Deligne cohomology \\cite{brylinski1}. Deligne",
