      "extract": "\\label{sec:path2groupoid} The basic idea of the path 2-groupoid is very simple: for a smooth manifold $X$, it is a strict 2-category whose objects are the points of $X$, whose 1-morphisms are smooth paths in~$X$, and whose 2-morphisms are smooth homotopies between these paths. We recall some definitions from \\cite{schreiber3,schreiber5}. For points $x,y\\in X$, a \\emph{path} $\\gamma:x \\to y$ is a smooth map",
